cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper."
title: "Feedback-Learning-Based Polarimetric Scattering Representation for PolSAR Ship Detection"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a feedback-learning pipeline for PolSAR ship
  detection: a lightweight MLP teacher distils pixel-level hard labels into a
  continuous ship-membership surface, and an evolutionary symbolic-regression
  student fits a closed-form polarimetric descriptor under an explicit
  accuracy-complexity trade-off. The repository covers the six-node descriptor,
  the eight-detector comparison, the operator and soft-label ablations, and the
  IPSD cross-sensor check with one scalar calibration.
